{"term":"encounter","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:e42bcfd9db63afe431","definition":"To meet (someone) or find (something), especially unexpectedly.","example":"It fits Ioues ſonne / VVraſtle vvith Lyons, and to tugge vvith Beares, / Grapple vvith Dragons, and incounter VVhales.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["cross paths"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["encounterable","encounterer","misencounter","nonencounter","reencounter","re-encounter","unencountered"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/encounter#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bc1590d5f98d71191a","definition":"To confront (someone or something) face to face.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["encounterable","encounterer","misencounter","nonencounter","reencounter","re-encounter","unencountered"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/encounter#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a1467fe22b74903504","definition":"To meet one another.","example":"[…] yet when the brother and the sister had encountered, according to the set appointment, none of these impassionedments had been repeated.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"rare","register":"intransitive, rare","wordFamily":["encounterable","encounterer","misencounter","nonencounter","reencounter","re-encounter","unencountered"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/encounter#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4f6ad093bc55bf8e7d","definition":"To engage in conflict, as with an enemy.","example":"Three armies encountered at Waterloo.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["encounterable","encounterer","misencounter","nonencounter","reencounter","re-encounter","unencountered"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/encounter#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b9fd19b8e9c3ff34e3","definition":"To kill or execute someone extrajudicially.","example":"Speaking to the media, Reddy said, \"He (Accused in 6-year-old rape and murder case) should be encountered. We will nab the accused and will encounter him. We will stand by the victim's family. We console them and will provide aid to the family. We will encounter him (the accused).\"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"India, euphemistic","register":"India, euphemistic, transitive","wordFamily":["encounterable","encounterer","misencounter","nonencounter","reencounter","re-encounter","unencountered"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/encounter#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3a7d49eb1d4131584e","definition":"A meeting, especially one that is unplanned or unexpected.","example":"Their encounter was a matter of chance.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["encounterable","encounterer","misencounter","nonencounter","reencounter","re-encounter","unencountered","close encounter","encounter group","marriage encounter","random encounter"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/encounter#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1677351d246db08f09","definition":"A hostile, often violent meeting; a confrontation, skirmish, or clash, as between combatants.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["clash","confrontation","brush","skirmish"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["encounterable","encounterer","misencounter","nonencounter","reencounter","re-encounter","unencountered","close encounter","encounter group","marriage encounter","random encounter"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/encounter#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3f1c6a7d68e4c441ab","definition":"A match between two opposing sides.","example":"Andre Santos equalised and the outstanding Theo Walcott put Arsenal ahead for the first time before Juan Mata's spectacular strike set up the finale for an enthralling encounter.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["encounterable","encounterer","misencounter","nonencounter","reencounter","re-encounter","unencountered","close encounter","encounter group","marriage encounter","random encounter"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/encounter#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0dfde0502e7e3d4ff1","definition":"A sexual encounter; sexual activity, especially unplanned or unexpected, between two people who have not already established a sexual relationship with each other. In many cases, it does not lead to a relationship, and thus is utterly transient. A sexual encounter can be consensual or non-consensual; in the latter case, it is known as sexual assault. A consensual sexual encounter that happens only once is commonly known as a one-night stand.","example":"Though Mr. Cosby described the sexual encounter in 2004 as consensual, Ms. Constand said she was too intoxicated to physically or verbally resist.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["encounterable","encounterer","misencounter","nonencounter","reencounter","re-encounter","unencountered","close encounter","encounter group","marriage encounter","random encounter"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/encounter#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b7f87be6379d34d4d4","definition":"The period of a space mission during which it carries out its data-gathering objectives.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["encounterable","encounterer","misencounter","nonencounter","reencounter","re-encounter","unencountered","close encounter","encounter group","marriage encounter","random encounter"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/encounter#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:50b95d5c7f98d7bd1b","definition":"An extrajudicial killing or execution.","example":"Telangana Labour and Employment Minister Malla Reddy on Tuesday said that the guilty person in the rape and murder of a six-year-old girl in Hyderabad \"will be nabbed and will be killed in an encounter\".","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"India","register":"India","wordFamily":["encounterable","encounterer","misencounter","nonencounter","reencounter","re-encounter","unencountered","close encounter","encounter group","marriage encounter","random encounter"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/encounter#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ɪnˈkaʊntə/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/d/d6/En-us-encounter.ogg/En-us-encounter.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["encounterable","encounterer","misencounter","nonencounter","reencounter","re-encounter","unencountered","close encounter",